  <section class="mp-section" id="calling-process"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">01 / The operating detail</p><h2>A calling campaign<br>takes more than dial time.</h2><p>As your outsourced cold calling agency, we agree the preparation, execution and feedback loop your campaign needs.</p></div><ol class="mp-call-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Prepare the audience and conversation.</h3><p>Define accounts, buyer roles and exclusions. Review usable contact records, the reason for calling, likely objections and what should qualify a meeting.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Make the calls. Listen to the answer.</h3><p>People open the conversation, check the relevance and ask questions. Technology can support research and workflow; the caller responds to the buyer.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Work the appropriate follow-up.</h3><p>Handle requested information, callbacks and referrals. Record a clear next action, or close the record when the account does not fit or asks for contact to stop.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Qualify, schedule and review.</h3><p>Confirm the purpose of a relevant meeting and prepare the agreed notes. Review buyer responses and sales feedback to improve the audience and talk track.</p></div></li></ol><p class="mp-caption">Agree territories, calling coverage, contact requirements, opt-out handling and responsibilities before launch. Data preparation and CRM work belong in the scope.</p><div class="mp-tool-band"><div><h3>See a starting approach to your buyers.</h3><p>Choose your offer and market to explore the conversation and related CallTeam resources.</p></div><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">See How We’d Run Your Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="conversation"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">02 / The conversation in practice</p><h2>A useful question<br>opens more than a pitch.</h2><p class="mp-section-lead">An opener should give the buyer enough context to confirm, correct or reject the reason for the call.</p><p>For a manufacturing software campaign, the starting question might concern how order changes reach the shop floor. The caller then follows the actual response.</p><p>Discussing the existing process can reveal a relevant problem, a different contact or a reason to leave the account alone. A meeting follows only when there is a useful discussion to have.</p><a class="mp-text-link" href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/">Browse 100 B2B cold calling scripts →</a><div class="mp-inline-tool"><h3>Already have an opening?</h3><p>Use the free checker to review the wording and find related examples.</p><a class="mp-button" href="/cold-call-script-checker/">Check Your Cold Call Script <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="mp-dialogue" aria-labelledby="mp-dialogue-heading"><p class="mp-label">Illustrative conversation / software offer</p><h3 id="mp-dialogue-heading">Listen for the real situation.</h3><div class="mp-speech"><span>Caller</span><p>“We help manufacturers keep production teams up to date when orders change. How does a change get from your planning system to the people on the floor?”</p></div><div class="mp-speech mp-speech-buyer"><span>Buyer</span><p>“We already have an ERP.”</p></div><div class="mp-speech"><span>Caller</span><p>“Understood. Does it carry changes all the way through, or does someone still update the floor separately?”</p></div><p class="mp-small">A fictional example of a follow-up question. It is not a recording, customer quotation or prescribed script.</p></aside></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section" id="reporting"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">03 / Know what the activity means</p><h2>Follow the campaign<br>past the call count.</h2><p>The review should explain where accounts move and where the work needs to change.</p></div><div class="mp-report-grid"><article><p class="mp-label">Audience coverage</p><h3>Are we reaching<br>the right market?</h3><p>Review account fit, usable contacts, attempts and routing. Poor data and the wrong audience need different responses.</p></article><article><p class="mp-label">Live conversations</p><h3>What are buyers<br>telling us?</h3><p>Track useful discussions, objections, referrals and timing. Use those responses to assess the message and contact path.</p></article><article><p class="mp-label">Qualified meetings</p><h3>Why did the buyer<br>agree to talk?</h3><p>Keep the account fit, role, business reason and meeting purpose visible. Record unanswered questions for sales.</p></article><article><p class="mp-label">Sales progression</p><h3>What happened<br>after the booking?</h3><p>Separate booked, held, sales-accepted and opportunity stages. Review the reasons meetings fail to progress.</p></article></div><div class="mp-tool-band"><div><h3>Make the meeting standard explicit.</h3><p>Use a real booking cohort to examine attendance, acceptance and opportunity creation.</p></div><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Use the Meeting Quality Check <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section mp-proof" id="calling-proof"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">04 / Calling in real B2B markets</p><h2>The result needs<br>the campaign behind it.</h2><p>See how targeting, questions, qualification and follow-through worked for these offers.</p></div>{% set proofCases = [commercialServices.cases[0], commercialServices.cases[2]] %}{% include "commercial/proof.njk" %}<div class="mp-experience"><div><strong>500,000+</strong><span>outbound calls</span></div><div><strong>1,000+</strong><span>sellers coached</span></div><div><strong>150+</strong><span>companies supported</span></div><div><strong>Fortune 100/500</strong><span>sales experience</span></div></div><p class="mp-proof-note">Combined professional experience behind CallTeam. <a href="/about/">Learn about the people and approach →</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section" id="calling-cost"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">05 / Price the work you actually need</p><h2>Calling coverage.<br>Clear scope.</h2><p class="mp-price">From US$4,000<span> / month</span></p><p>That is the starting rate for a campaign-ready managed program: a defined B2B offer and market, usable accounts or contacts, CRM and calendar access, and sellers ready to handle meetings.</p><p>New research, licensed data, additional markets and extra resources affect the final proposal. Most programs begin with an initial three-month engagement.</p><p><a href="/pricing/">Review current pricing</a> and <a href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">model your campaign economics</a>.</p></div><aside class="mp-fit-note"><h3>Where this engagement fits</h3><p>Choose a managed calling campaign when you know which businesses can benefit from your offer and need a team to reach them consistently.</p><ul class="mp-checks"><li>Your service needs a business conversation.</li><li>The buyer and account criteria can be defined.</li><li>Sales is ready for the next step.</li></ul><p>For a broader account-to-meeting engagement, explore <a href="/services/b2b-lead-generation/">B2B lead generation services</a>. For ongoing management of a wider sales development function, see <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">outsourced SDR services</a>.</p></aside></div><div class="mp-wrap"><p class="mp-caption">Planning an internal campaign? The <a href="/articles/b2b-cold-calling-strategy/">B2B cold calling strategy guide</a> explains the operating choices. Our <a href="/b2b-cold-calling-campaign-process/">calling campaign process</a> sets out the preparation and review stages.</p></div></section>
